    Samangan Province is located in the northern part of Afghanistan. It is bordered by Baghlan to the East,
    Bamyan to the South, Sar-e-Pul to the South-West, Balkh Province to the West and Kunduz to the North
    Text Box 1 Median Age
    (Figure 1). The province lies at the coordinates 36.1°N, 68.1°E (CSO, 2015). It is well positioned on the
    main trade road between Mazar-e-Sharif and Pul-e-Khumri, Salang and Kabul.

